#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Pop-Piece Puzzle
A small Tkinter GUI with the 60 preset challenges from the booklet.

Run with:
    python pop_piece_puzzle.py

Goal: slide the RED piece onto the EXIT square at the upper-right.

Controls:
- Pick a challenge from the drop-down at the top. "Reset Board" puts the
  current challenge back to its starting layout (and clears the timer).
- The timer starts automatically when you move the first piece and stops
  when the red piece reaches the exit.
- Pieces SLIDE on the board, like the real game: drag a piece and it follows
  the pointer one square at a time, stopping when it hits a wall or another
  piece. You can't lift a piece and drop it somewhere else, and a piece can't
  squeeze diagonally between two pieces. The upper-right EXIT square can only
  be entered straight from the left.
- The white pieces are locked, as in the real game: they cannot be moved
  or rotated.
- Rotation is switched off because pieces only slide in the real game.
  (Set ALLOW_ROTATION = True below to bring back right-click / R rotation.)
"""
